From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:00:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: no two-pane layout below the split smallest width
 (Titan 2)

Activity embedding checks window bounds, not the configuration; require
the configuration's smallestScreenWidthDp (capped by the framework via
persist.sys.titan2.max_sw_dp) to reach config_activity_embed_split_min_sw_dp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../settings/activityembedding/ActivityEmbeddingUtils.java    | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/activityembedding/ActivityEmbeddingUtils.java b/src/com/android/settings/activityembedding/ActivityEmbeddingUtils.java
index 75ab087..b9e4d88 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/activityembedding/ActivityEmbeddingUtils.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/activityembedding/ActivityEmbeddingUtils.java
@@ -84,6 +84,10 @@ public class ActivityEmbeddingUtils {
      */
     public static boolean isSettingsSplitEnabled(Context context) {
         return SHOULD_ENABLE_LARGE_SCREEN_OPTIMIZATION
+                // Titan 2: no two-pane layout when the framework caps smallestScreenWidthDp
+                // (persist.sys.titan2.max_sw_dp) to keep the phone UI at low density.
+                && context.getResources().getConfiguration().smallestScreenWidthDp
+                        >= getMinSmallestScreenSplitWidthDp(context)
                 && SplitController.getInstance(context).getSplitSupportStatus()
                 == SplitController.SplitSupportStatus.SPLIT_AVAILABLE;
     }
-- 
